{"content_id":"CL-SHF-FUND-L11-ENVIRONMENT","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-OUT","D-FLD"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"1.1","block_identifier":"environment-context","question_identifier":"q11","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"The same equipment or task can present different risks when surface, weather, visibility, traffic, access or other environmental conditions change; the worker should re-orient to the actual route and assigned method rather than assuming yesterday's conditions still apply.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"awareness_only","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Environment changes risk/context; no specific handling procedure is established by this claim."}
{"content_id":"CL-SHF-FUND-L13-ASSIGNMENT-CONTROL","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-COM"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"1.3","block_identifier":"conflicting-instructions","question_identifier":"q13","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"When instructions conflict, the learner should resolve the change through the person/process controlling the current assignment rather than choosing whichever instruction sounds most authoritative.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Exact title may be lead, steward, department head or another designated work-control role."}
{"content_id":"CL-SHF-FUND-L42-DIRECTIONS","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-VOP","D-SMG"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"4","lesson_identifier":"4.2","block_identifier":"stage-house-directions","question_identifier":"q42","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Stage left/right use the performer's perspective facing the audience, while house left/right use the audience/house perspective facing the stage; local venue terminology can add additional location conventions.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"awareness_only","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Exact external terminology source should be added during low-risk citation backfill; current internal audit supports the convention."}
{"content_id":"CL-SHF-FUND-L53-CORRECTION","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-CAR","D-COM"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"5","lesson_identifier":"5.3","block_identifier":"professional-correction","question_identifier":"q63","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A reliable worker responds to correction by acknowledging the work-control issue, changing unsafe or incorrect behavior as needed and seeking clarification without turning active work into an argument; exact supervisory/disciplinary procedures remain employer/local specific.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"professional_conduct","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Professionalism pattern, not a universal rule that every correction is correct or that workers waive reporting/appeal rights."}
{"content_id":"Q-SHF-FUND-Q11","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-OUT","D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"1.1","block_identifier":"environment-context","question_identifier":"q11","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"The same case moves from an indoor environment to uneven outdoor ground. Correct answer: environmental conditions change risk, so confirm the actual path and assigned control method rather than assuming nothing changed.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"awareness_only","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Tests context recognition, not a specific outdoor handling technique."}
{"content_id":"QR-SHF-FUND-Q11","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-OUT","D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"1.1","block_identifier":"environment-context-coaching","question_identifier":"q11","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Familiar equipment does not erase new route, surface, weather or visibility conditions; re-orient to the actual work environment and controlling method.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"awareness_only","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-SHF-FUND-L11-ENVIRONMENT."}
{"content_id":"Q-SHF-FUND-Q12","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"1.2","block_identifier":"phase-context","question_identifier":"q12","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"An item is positioned differently during show than during load-in. Correct answer: the phase may make that placement intentional; do not change it without direction.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"awareness_only","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Tests phase/context awareness."}
{"content_id":"QR-SHF-FUND-Q12","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"1.2","block_identifier":"phase-context-coaching","question_identifier":"q12","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Load-in, performance/show support and load-out are distinct operational phases; equipment state and placement can change with the phase, so appearance alone does not authorize changes.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"awareness_only","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-SHF-FUND-M01-BASE."}
{"content_id":"Q-SHF-FUND-Q13","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-COM","D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"1.3","block_identifier":"conflicting-instructions","question_identifier":"q13","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"The assigned lead says to leave cases closed and another person gives a conflicting instruction. Correct answer: confirm the change through the controlling assignment process before acting.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Tests assignment ownership and conflict resolution."}
{"content_id":"QR-SHF-FUND-Q13","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-COM","D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"1.3","block_identifier":"conflicting-instructions-coaching","question_identifier":"q13","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Conflicting work instructions are resolved through the person/process controlling the current assignment so the crew does not create competing work states.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-SHF-FUND-L13-ASSIGNMENT-CONTROL."}
{"content_id":"Q-SHF-FUND-Q41","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-OUT","D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"4","lesson_identifier":"4.1","block_identifier":"orient-before-action","question_identifier":"q41","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A worker enters a new venue near an active unload. Correct answer: check in, identify the controlling lead/process and orient to traffic/hazards before joining work rather than self-assigning immediately.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"work_readiness","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Tests orientation sequence as a recurring pattern, not a universal literal 15-minute rule."}
{"content_id":"QR-SHF-FUND-Q41","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-OUT","D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"4","lesson_identifier":"4.1","block_identifier":"orient-before-action-coaching","question_identifier":"q41","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Orientation establishes reporting structure, routes, equipment traffic and controlled zones before the worker joins the task; exact check-in timing and sequence remain call-specific.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"work_readiness","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-SHF-FUND-M04-BASE and SFS-O01 evidence."}
{"content_id":"Q-SHF-FUND-Q42","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-VOP","D-SMG","D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"4","lesson_identifier":"4.2","block_identifier":"stage-directions","question_identifier":"q42","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A worker stands in the house facing the stage and is directed to stage left. Correct answer: use the performer's left while facing the audience, which appears on the worker's right from the house-facing-stage position.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"awareness_only","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Terminology question; exact primary terminology citation remains a low-risk backfill item."}
{"content_id":"QR-SHF-FUND-Q42","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-VOP","D-SMG","D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"4","lesson_identifier":"4.2","block_identifier":"stage-directions-coaching","question_identifier":"q42","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Stage left/right use performer perspective; house left/right use house/audience perspective. If local terminology is unclear, the worker should clarify rather than guess.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"awareness_only","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-SHF-FUND-L42-DIRECTIONS."}
{"content_id":"Q-SHF-FUND-Q63","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-CAR","D-COM","D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"5","lesson_identifier":"5.3","block_identifier":"professional-correction","question_identifier":"q63","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A lead corrects the worker sharply during active work. Correct answer: acknowledge and correct any immediate safety/process issue, remain professional and seek clarification appropriately rather than escalating the conflict during the task.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"professional_conduct","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Does not imply that workers lose rights to report misconduct, unsafe orders or disputes through appropriate channels."}
{"content_id":"QR-SHF-FUND-Q63","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-CAR","D-COM","D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"5","lesson_identifier":"5.3","block_identifier":"professional-correction-coaching","question_identifier":"q63","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Professional correction behavior means preserving active work control and addressing the immediate issue without unnecessary argument; formal concerns or unsafe directions can still be escalated through the appropriate process.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"professional_conduct","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-SHF-FUND-L53-CORRECTION."}